/// EtsTid — an opaque `ets:tid()` table identifier.
///
/// Erlang's `ets:new/2` answers a tid and every other `ets` call takes one
/// back. The checker types those FFI results with this class so the table
/// identifier stays a named type (rather than `Dynamic`).
///
/// An EtsTid has no protocol of its own: its contents are not inspectable, and
/// sending it any message other than the `Object` protocol (identity and
/// equality such as `=:=`) is a type error. For ordinary table work use `Ets`.
///
/// This is an opaque-handle class in the "Object" kind of the three-kind
/// model (ADR 0067): no `state:`/`field:` slots and not instantiable from
/// Beamtalk. It is declared only so FFI specs have a type to name.
///
/// The class is static only: at run time the value is a Reference, so `x class` answers
/// that and `x isKindOf:` against this class is always false.
/// Node-scoped (ADR 0103): any process on the node can use a tid, but it is
/// meaningless on another node, so it is `#node`-scoped like `Ets` itself —
/// silent in v1 unless the receiver is known to be remote.
sealed typed Object subclass: EtsTid
  handleScope: #node
